From fe192413b090051de30472bb77447a886a451d57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Picocom <support@picocom.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_dpaa: support 1000base-x on FMan MEMAC

The SDK FMan MAC API maps the Linux PHY interface mode to an SDK
enet_mode_t using the _1000 table.  PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_1000BASEX was
missing from this table, causing an out-of-bounds array access.  In
practice this could select the 10G mode and make a 1G MEMAC fail with
"10G MAC ID must be less than 2".

Map 1000BASE-X to the SDK's existing SGMII/BASE-X 1G mode.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor SDK driver fix]
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/mac-api.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/mac-api.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/mac-api.c
index bb0c4e49182c..4601e3a76539 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/mac-api.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/mac-api.c
@@ -86,6 +86,7 @@ static const enet_mode_t _1000[] = {
 	[PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII]	= e_ENET_MODE_SGMII_1000,
 	[PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_QSGMII]	= e_ENET_MODE_QSGMII_1000,
 	[PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_TBI]	= e_ENET_MODE_TBI_1000,
+	[PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_1000BASEX] = e_ENET_MODE_SGMII_BASEX_1000,
 	[PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII]	= e_ENET_MODE_RGMII_1000,
 	[PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_ID]	= e_ENET_MODE_RGMII_1000,
 	[PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_RXID]	= e_ENET_MODE_RGMII_1000,
